}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({e}^{y}-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking  $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{g}^{′}(y) & =x{e}^{y}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =0 \\\\ g(y) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-132079" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "12b7d1b64dd7cdd68f7177ee05fb7129c16fc63fa5ad07a171a784baabdb59b7"} {"question" "q-132079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-132079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=y{e}^{y}+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)={x}^{2}{e}^{y}+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)={y}^{2}{e}^{y}+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-132079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-81734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f=F,$ where $F(x,y)=(2x{y}^{2}+1)\\,i+(2{x}^{2}y+1)\\,j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-81734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x{y}^{2}+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}y+1\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2x{y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}y+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}y+1$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}y+{g}^{′}(y) & =2{x}^{2}y+1 \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =1 \\\\ g(y) & =y+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=y+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x+y+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-81734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "12b7d1b64dd7cdd68f7177ee05fb7129c16fc63fa5ad07a171a784baabdb59b7"} {"question" "q-81734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-81734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=4xy+xy+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x+y+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+y+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-81734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x+y+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-132077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f=F,$ where $F(x,y)=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+y)\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+x)\\,j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-132077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+x\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+xy+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+x+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking  $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+x$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+x+{g}^{′}(y) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+x \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =0 \\\\ g(y) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+xy+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-132077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "12b7d1b64dd7cdd68f7177ee05fb7129c16fc63fa5ad07a171a784baabdb59b7"} {"question" "q-132077" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-132077" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}y+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+x+y+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+xy+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+{y}^{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-132077" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+xy+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-81748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f=F,$ where $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-81748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking  $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{g}^{′}(y) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ g(y) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046299/state.json" "file_sha256" "664c698c201658a8fa9bd4c5b315fd03bc3ce8c35e49e9e65cd91a37a6a91041"} {"question" "q-81748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-w